unordered-list-style (MD004), Lists
On by default, severity warning. Fixable.
Your configuration sets its severity to info.
ul-style is markdownlint's name for this rule.

Every bullet uses the same marker as the first bullet in the file.

Why: Mixed markers make the source harder to read. Inside a list, a different
marker also starts a new list.

Tags: bullet, ul

Options, under rules.unordered-list-style.options:
  style (string, default consistent)
    Bullet to require. consistent takes the bullet of the first list, and
    sublist gives each nesting level a bullet that differs from its parent
    level's. Values: consistent, asterisk, plus, dash, sublist.

Fix: The fix changes each marker to the expected one. gomdlint reports a list
without a fix when the new marker would merge it with a list next to it.
gomdlint may report a finding without a fix when the fix would change a line
with one character in brackets, such as [x] or [1], or the lines around it up to
a blank line, because it could add or remove a task list checkbox. In a document
with raw HTML other than comments and plain br, wbr, hr or img tags, gomdlint
reports every finding without a fix.

This document breaks the rule:
  | # Requirements
  |
  | - Go
  |   * Version 1.24 or later
  | - Make

gomdlint reports:
  4:3 Unordered list bullet '*' does not match expected '-'

The fix changes it to:
  | # Requirements
  |
  | - Go
  |   - Version 1.24 or later
  | - Make

Configure:
  rules:
    unordered-list-style:
      options:
        style: consistent

Under rules, unordered-list-style: false turns the rule off and
unordered-list-style: error reports its findings as errors. The flag
--disable unordered-list-style turns it off for one run.

Silence one line:
  <!-- markdownlint-disable-next-line ul-style -->

markdownlint: https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint/blob/v0.41.1/doc/md004.md
